---
// B2.DETAILS — design §5 "Disclosure", IA I-12, deck §5 `agree`.
//
// Native `<details>`/`<summary>`: real DOM text, crawlable, no fetch, and the panel's height
// is never animated at any setting. The summary is a noun phrase, and it has a hover state
// because a summary with none is the one control on the page that never answers a pointer.
//
// R-17 constrains the body: static text until an `agreement.json` exists, and the only
// numerals permitted in it are the ones with a §4.3 slot row — so the target name is
// interpolated from `facts` rather than typed, like every other numeral on the page.
import { facts } from '../lib/examples.ts'

const BODY =
  'The oracle executes the authored module on a CPU in double precision, from the same ' +
  'source the emitters read. The compile gate emits every registered example, creates a ' +
  'shader module from each WGSL emit on Tint, and compiles and links both ' +
  `${facts.glslTarget} stages of every renderable example on a real WebGL2 context; it ` +
  'proves that instrument on a deliberately broken shader before it trusts a pass. The ' +
  'goldens diff every emit byte for ' +
  'byte against a committed file. No pixel comparison between the two backends is committed ' +
  'yet, so none is printed here.'
---

{/* Server-rendered OPEN: the panel is evidence, and with no JS it must be readable and
    crawlable. I-12 asks for it COLLAPSED below 1024, which no CSS can do to a `<details>` —
    so one inline statement closes it there, before first paint, and its failure mode is the
    safe one (the text stays visible). */}
<details open>
  <summary class="summary">
    <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    How this was measured
  </summary>
  <p class="text-meta max-w-[var(--measure-body)] pb-2 text-text-2">{BODY}</p>
</details>

<script is:inline>
  // Runs where it is parsed, so the panel is never seen open and then shut (no height
  // animation at any setting — design §6).
  if (window.matchMedia('(max-width: 63.99rem)').matches) {
    document.currentScript.previousElementSibling.open = false
  }
</script>
